Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:16:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Shaders: join straddling global 16-bit loads across dwords

A root-SRV global_load_ushort/sshort at byte 3 mod 4 dropped its high
byte. Join the next dword's low byte, and reuse the first dword for
non-straddling loads. Keep the existing sign extension and byte loads.
Bump the translator version so cached translations do not hide the fix.

The boundary join follows the buffer-load fix in Marvisak/VIctory#3333
(80e8cede); this applies it to this branch's separate global-load path.
Add synthetic GPU coverage for both signednesses and both wave sizes,
with byte-load controls at every byte alignment.

Implementation and testing assisted by OpenAI Codex.
